{"step_index":705,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-24T20:02:18Z","input_tokens":6451,"cache_read_tokens":68443,"output_tokens":1361,"thinking":"Initial examination of the provided evidence suggests a focus on customer data and resource management, spanning several dates. There's a potential area of concern surrounding database replicas and a customer account handover, which necessitates a deeper look at the logs to understand any potential dependencies or anomalies. The service resource export may provide context on the overall infrastructure being used.\n\n\nThe analysis reveals a strong mapping between cases and primary evidence files, with almost every case traceable to a single source. An exception highlights a possible dependency on two distinct evidence files for a particular case. This mapping indicates the primary data source for each case's conclusions is readily identifiable. This pattern suggests a streamlined approach to tracing the origins of any reported findings.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"import csv\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nwith open(\"dataset/sample_output.csv\", encoding=\"utf-8-sig\") as f:\n    expected = {r[\"case_id\"]: r for r in csv.DictReader(f)}\n\ndataset_dir = Path(\"dataset\")\n\nfor cid in sorted(expected.keys()):\n    steps = json.loads(expected[cid][\"steps_json\"])\n    # find all resources in steps\n    for s in steps:\n        res = s[\"resource_id\"]\n        ev = s[\"evidence_id\"]\n        # let's see which files contain this resource\n        matching_files = []\n        for p in (dataset_dir / \"evidence\").rglob(\"*\"):\n            if p.is_file():\n                try:\n                    txt = p.read_text(\"utf-8\", \"ignore\")\n                    if res in txt:\n                        matching_files.append(p.name)\n                except:\n                    pass\n        print(f\"{cid} | {s['phase']} | {s['system_id']} |